Output

Flags:
  -o, --output FORMAT           One of auto, json, values, table, raw, csv, tsv or
                                markdown.
  -r, --raw                     Print only the answer value or policy decision.
      --merge                   Keep input fields and attach the answers.
  -V, --version                 Print the version, commit, build date and built in
                                limits, as one JSON object under -o json.
      --out FILE                Write the answers to this file rather than stdout.
      --merge-key KEY           Put the answers under this key in the merged record.
                                Implies --merge.
      --usage                   Add the API usage object to JSON output.
      --stats                   Write a one line summary of the run to stderr at exit.
  -h, --help                    Show this help.

How they work together:
  Auto uses a table only for one result on a terminal, without --merge or --out. It uses
  JSON when redirected, for streams, for merged records and for --out files. --raw
  selects raw output. Raw prints the policy decision when present, otherwise the answer
  value, and does not preserve the original record.

  --merge keeps the input fields and places answer metadata under answers by default.
  --merge-key selects another location and implies --merge. JSON preserves model values,
  decisions and errors. A request error remains in the output even when a fallback
  supplies a decision. --out writes answers to a file instead of stdout. See Execution
  for resume and pruning. --usage adds API usage to JSON output. --stats writes a one
  line run summary to stderr at exit. --version prints the version, commit, build date
  and built in limits, as one JSON object with -o json.

